      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "The receiving operator needs observable results, not the author’s memory.",
          "role": "intro",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#tb1"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "A runbook records procedures for a known operational outcome and should be usable by the operator doing the task.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#f1"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#tb2"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Make preconditions, action order and expected results explicit so the operator checks execution instead of inferring it.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#f2"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#tb3"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Include failure handling and escalation: state when routine work stops and identify who takes over.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#tb3"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "In the orders restart record, compare preconditions with the approved task before the restart. Check each expected result before advancing, including the supplied health result. Keep the stop condition and escalation recipient visible; do not invent a recovery action.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#f1",
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#f2",
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#tb4"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "An action list alone is insufficient. Preconditions, expected results and failure/escalation instructions make the task checkable.",
          "role": "misconception",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.hand_over_an_actionable_operational_runbook#f2",
